## 3. Iceberg Tracking & Observations

### BYU / US National Ice Center (USNIC) Antarctic Iceberg Tracking Database
- **Dataset name:** BYU Antarctic Iceberg Tracking Database (merged with USNIC Operational Iceberg Records)
- **Provider:** Brigham Young University (BYU) Center for Remote Sensing & U.S. National Ice Center (USNIC)
- **URL:** https://www.scp.byu.edu/data/iceberg/ & https://usicecenter.gov/Products/AntarcIcebergs
- **License:** Public Domain (U.S. Government Open Data)
- **Spatial resolution:** Point observation coordinates with measured bounding geometry (Length $\times$ Width)
- **Temporal resolution:** Daily to weekly tracking updates
- **Coordinate system:** Geographic coordinates WGS84 (EPSG:4326)
- **Variables:**
  - `iceberg_id`: Alphanumeric iceberg identifier (e.g., A-68A, B-15A)
  - `date` / `timestamp`: Date and time of observation (UTC)
  - `latitude`: Geographic latitude of iceberg centroid (decimal degrees)
  - `longitude`: Geographic longitude of iceberg centroid (decimal degrees)
  - `length`: Long axis dimension
  - `width`: Short axis dimension
  - `source`: Sensor or analyst source (e.g., Sentinel-1 SAR, MODIS, Scatterometer)
- **Units:**
  - Latitude / Longitude: Decimal degrees [$^\circ\text{S}, ^\circ\text{W/E}$]
  - Dimensions: Kilometers ($\text{km}$) or Nautical Miles ($\text{NM}$)
- **Missing-data representation:** Blank text fields, `None`, or sentinel values `-999`
- **Processing performed:**
  1. Text/CSV parsing and chronological sorting by iceberg identifier.
  2. Standardization of geometric dimensions into metric meters ($L, W$).
  3. Coordinate transformation from EPSG:4326 to EPSG:3031.
  4. Generation of spatial bounding polygons and dynamic Gaussian avoidance risk buffers.
- **Date downloaded:** *Not yet downloaded (Planned / Schema Defined)*

