## 5. Ocean Currents & Hydrodynamics

### Copernicus Marine Service (CMEMS) Global Ocean Physics Analysis and Forecast
- **Dataset name:** Global Ocean Physics Analysis and Forecast (`GLOBAL_ANALYSISFORECAST_PHY_001_024`)
- **Provider:** Copernicus Marine Service / Mercator Ocean International
- **URL:** https://marine.copernicus.eu/
- **License:** Open and free access under the Copernicus Marine Service Licence
- **Spatial resolution:** 1/12° horizontal resolution (approx. 8 km) across 50 vertical depth levels
- **Temporal resolution:** Daily means and hourly surface field updates
- **Coordinate system:** WGS84 Geographic Regular Lat/Lon (EPSG:4326)
- **Variables:**
  - `uo`: Eastward sea water velocity component
  - `vo`: Northward sea water velocity component
  - `zos`: Sea surface height above geoid
  - `thetao`: Sea water potential temperature
  - `so`: Sea water salinity
- **Units:**
  - Velocity components (`uo`, `vo`): Meters per second ($\text{m/s}$)
  - Sea surface height (`zos`): Meters ($\text{m}$)
  - Temperature (`thetao`): Degrees Celsius ($^\circ\text{C}$)
  - Salinity (`so`): Practical Salinity Units ($\text{PSU}$)
- **Missing-data representation:** NetCDF `_FillValue = 1.0e+20` or `NaN` (continental landmasses masked)
- **Processing performed:**
  1. Depth slicing for surface layer ($0\text{ m}$) and depth-integrated keel draft layers ($0 - 150\text{ m}$ for deep-keeled tabular icebergs).
  2. Reprojection of ocean current velocity vectors into EPSG:3031.
  3. Integration into hydrodynamic drag modules and vessel transit speed adjustment models.
- **Date downloaded:** *Not yet downloaded (Planned / Schema Defined)*

