## 6. Bathymetry

### GEBCO Gridded Bathymetric Data (GEBCO_2023 / GEBCO_2024)
- **Dataset name:** General Bathymetric Chart of the Oceans (GEBCO) 30-arc-second / 15-arc-second Grid
- **Provider:** GEBCO / International Hydrographic Organization (IHO) / UNESCO Intergovernmental Oceanographic Commission (IOC)
- **URL:** https://www.gebco.net/data_and_products/gridded_bathymetry_data/
- **License:** GEBCO Open Data Licence (Public use with attribution)
- **Spatial resolution:** 15 arc-second grid interval (approx. 450 m at the equator, converging poleward)
- **Temporal resolution:** Static / Periodic annual compilation releases
- **Coordinate system:** WGS84 Geographic coordinates (EPSG:4326)
- **Variables:**
  - `elevation`: Elevation / depth relative to Mean Sea Level (MSL)
- **Units:** Meters ($\text{m}$), where negative values denote submarine depth below sea level
- **Missing-data representation:** NetCDF `_FillValue = -32767` or `NaN`
- **Processing performed:**
  1. Spatial clipping below $-50^\circ\text{ S}$ latitude.
  2. Aggregation / downsampling to match target navigation grid cells ($5\text{ km} - 25\text{ km}$).
  3. Derivation of under-keel clearance masks: cells with $|\text{depth}| < \text{vessel\_draft} + \text{safety\_margin}$ are marked as non-navigable ($\text{Cost} = \infty$).
- **Date downloaded:** *Not yet downloaded (Planned / Schema Defined)*

