## 7. Coastlines & Continental Ice Boundaries

### SCAR Antarctic Digital Database (ADD) Coastlines & Ice Shelves
- **Dataset name:** SCAR Antarctic Digital Database (ADD) High-Resolution Topographic & Coastline Data
- **Provider:** Scientific Committee on Antarctic Research (SCAR) / British Antarctic Survey (BAS)
- **URL:** https://www.add.scar.org/
- **License:** Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
- **Spatial resolution:** Vector data at scales between 1:250,000 and 1:1,000,000
- **Temporal resolution:** Versioned periodic releases reflecting major calving and grounding-line updates
- **Coordinate system:** Antarctic Polar Stereographic (EPSG:3031) and WGS84 (EPSG:4326)
- **Variables:**
  - `surface`: Classification of terrain (`ice_shelf`, `grounded_ice`, `rock_exposure`, `open_water`)
  - `feature`: Geometric line/polygon type (`coastline`, `grounding_line`, `ice_front`)
- **Units:** Dimensionless categorical / vector geometries
- **Missing-data representation:** Empty feature attributes or null geometries
- **Processing performed:**
  1. Vector ingestion and geometry validation (closing unclosed rings, fixing self-intersections).
  2. Rasterization (burn-in) onto the discrete EPSG:3031 computation grid.
  3. Establishment of absolute hard-obstacle barriers ($\text{Cost} = \infty$) across all land and grounded ice zones.
- **Date downloaded:** *Not yet downloaded (Planned / Schema Defined)*
